      "beat_id": "NB11",
      "act": "5 DIRECTION B — ONE FLAG",
      "narration_text": "One flag: a formula can be pointed at the wrong cell entirely and never throw an error at all — because a DataFrame's row N lands one row lower in Excel, at row N plus one. Recalc.py can't catch a formula that's simply wrong, only one that's broken.",
